{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "deploy",
      "name": "Deployment controller",
      "watch": "watches Deployments"
    },
    {
      "id": "rs",
      "name": "ReplicaSet controller",
      "watch": "watches ReplicaSets and Pods"
    },
    {
      "id": "sched",
      "name": "Scheduler",
      "watch": "watches Pods with no node"
    },
    {
      "id": "eps",
      "name": "EndpointSlice controller",
      "watch": "watches Ready Pods for Services"
    }
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "happy",
      "tab": "Happy path",
      "short": "apply → Ready",
      "q": "From kubectl apply to a pod that receives traffic",
      "frames": [
        {
          "api": true,
          "term": "$ kubectl apply -f web.yaml\ndeployment.apps/web created\nservice/web created",
          "badge": "containers running: 0",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · image web:1.0",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: (none)",
              "st": "new"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "The API server stores the Deployment",
          "b": "It authenticates and authorizes the request, runs admission checks, validates the object and saves it to etcd. kubectl prints <code>created</code> and exits. Nothing is running yet."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "deploy": {
              "saw": "Deployment web, no ReplicaSet for it",
              "wrote": "ReplicaSet web-7d4b9 (replicas 3)"
            }
          },
          "badge": "containers running: 0",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · image web:1.0"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 0",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: (none)"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "Deployment controller",
          "b": "It sees a Deployment with no ReplicaSet and writes one. The suffix <code>7d4b9</code> is a hash of the pod template, so a different template gets a different ReplicaSet."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "rs": {
              "saw": "web-7d4b9 wants 3 pods, has 0",
              "wrote": "Pods -a1, -b2, -c3 (no node)"
            }
          },
          "badge": "containers running: 0",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: (none)"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "ReplicaSet controller",
          "b": "It compares desired (3) with actual (0) and writes three Pod objects. They have no node yet, so they are Pending. They are only records in the API server."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "sched": {
              "saw": "3 pods with no node",
              "wrote": "bindings: a1, b2 → node-1 · c3 → node-2"
            }
          },
          "badge": "containers running: 0",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: node-1 · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: node-1 · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: node-2 · Pending",
              "st": "new"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: (none)"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "Scheduler",
          "b": "For each pod it filters out nodes that can't fit its resource requests, scores the rest, and writes a binding. Still no container exists: the scheduler only decides where."
        },
        {
          "kub": {
            "node-1": {
              "saw": "a1, b2 bound to me",
              "wrote": "started containers · status Running"
            },
            "node-2": {
              "saw": "c3 bound to me",
              "wrote": "started container · status Running"
            }
          },
          "badge": "containers running: 3 · serving: 0",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node-1 · Running · 10.1.0.4"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node-1 · Running · 10.1.0.5"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node-2 · Running · 10.1.1.7"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: (none)"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": [
                {
                  "n": "a1",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "running",
                  "ip": "10.1.0.4",
                  "nw": 1
                },
                {
                  "n": "b2",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "running",
                  "ip": "10.1.0.5",
                  "nw": 1
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": [
                {
                  "n": "c3",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "running",
                  "ip": "10.1.1.7",
                  "nw": 1
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "h": "Kubelets start containers",
          "b": "Each kubelet sees pods bound to its node, asks the container runtime to pull the image and start the containers, and the network plugin gives each pod an IP. While the image downloads the pod is still Pending; then it is Running. Running is not yet Ready."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "eps": {
              "saw": "a1, b2, c3 Ready, match Service web",
              "wrote": "endpoints: 10.1.0.4, 10.1.0.5, 10.1.1.7"
            }
          },
          "badge": "containers running: 3 · serving: 3",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · available: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · ready: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node-1 · Ready"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node-1 · Ready"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node-2 · Ready"
            },
            {
              "k": "Service",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "endpoints: 10.1.0.4, 10.1.0.5, 10.1.1.7",
              "st": "new"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "pods": [
                {
                  "n": "a1",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "ready",
                  "ip": "10.1.0.4"
                },
                {
                  "n": "b2",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "ready",
                  "ip": "10.1.0.5"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "pods": [
                {
                  "n": "c3",
                  "img": "web:1.0",
                  "st": "ready",
                  "ip": "10.1.1.7"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "h": "Ready, then traffic",
          "b": "When the readiness probe passes, the kubelet reports the pod Ready. The EndpointSlice controller adds its IP to Service <code>web</code>. Only now does traffic reach it."
        }
      ],
      "take": "apply only records intent. The cluster converges on it through a chain of independent loops, connected only by objects in the API server.",
      "gen": "Declarative systems generally. Terraform also diffs desired against actual state, but only when you run it; Kubernetes runs the diff continuously. Operators use the same controller pattern."
    },
    {
      "id": "pending",
      "tab": "Scenario 1",
      "short": "Pending forever",
      "q": "The pod has been Pending for ten minutes and nothing has errored. What's wrong?",
      "frames": [
        {
          "api": true,
          "term": "$ kubectl apply -f web.yaml\ndeployment.apps/web created",
          "badge": "apply: success",
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · requests cpu: 4"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "Apply succeeds",
          "b": "The object is valid, so the API server accepts it. The Deployment and ReplicaSet controllers do their jobs exactly as in the happy path: three Pod objects exist."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "sched": {
              "saw": "3 pods with no node",
              "wrote": "event FailedScheduling · PodScheduled=False (Unschedulable)"
            }
          },
          "badge": "0/2 nodes are available: 2 Insufficient cpu",
          "bad": true,
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · requests cpu: 4"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · pods: 3"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending · Unschedulable",
              "st": "bad"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending · Unschedulable",
              "st": "bad"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending · Unschedulable",
              "st": "bad"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "No node fits",
          "b": "Filtering removes both nodes for insufficient CPU. The scheduler records a FailedScheduling event on each pod and marks it Unschedulable. It doesn't fail or delete anything."
        },
        {
          "kub": {
            "node-1": {
              "saw": "no pods bound to me",
              "wrote": "nothing"
            },
            "node-2": {
              "saw": "no pods bound to me",
              "wrote": "nothing"
            }
          },
          "badge": "no container, no crash, no restarts",
          "bad": true,
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · available: 0"
            },
            {
              "k": "ReplicaSet",
              "n": "web-7d4b9",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · ready: 0"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "Nothing else happens",
          "b": "No kubelet sees these pods, because none is bound to a node. There is no container to crash and no log to read. <code>kubectl describe pod</code> and its events are the only place the reason appears."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "sched": {
              "saw": "still 3 unschedulable pods",
              "wrote": "requeued · retries when the cluster changes"
            }
          },
          "badge": "waiting for capacity",
          "bad": true,
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "replicas: 3 · available: 0"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "The scheduler keeps retrying",
          "b": "It retries when the cluster changes: a node joins, another pod is deleted. If a cluster autoscaler is installed, it sees the unschedulable pods and adds a node big enough; then the scheduler places them."
        },
        {
          "on": {
            "deploy": {
              "saw": "no progress for 600 s",
              "wrote": "condition Progressing=False · ProgressDeadlineExceeded"
            }
          },
          "term": "$ kubectl rollout status deployment/web\n… fails: progress deadline exceeded",
          "badge": "reported, not rolled back",
          "bad": true,
          "objs": [
            {
              "k": "Deployment",
              "n": "web",
              "f": "available: 0 · Progressing=False (ProgressDeadlineExceeded)",
              "st": "bad"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-a1",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-b2",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            },
            {
              "k": "Pod",
              "n": "web-7d4b9-c3",
              "f": "node: — · Pending"
            }
          ],
          "nodes": [
            {
              "n": "node-1",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            },
            {
              "n": "node-2",
              "cap": "~2 CPU free",
              "pods": []
            }
          ],
          "h": "The Deployment finally reports it",
          "b": "After <code>progressDeadlineSeconds</code> (600 s by default) without progress, the Deployment's <code>Progressing</code> condition turns False with reason <code>ProgressDeadlineExceeded</code>. In CI, wait on <code>kubectl rollout status</code>, not on <code>apply</code>."
        }
      ],
      "take": "In a declarative system, success means \"accepted\", not \"done\". Look at pod events with kubectl describe, and gate deploys on kubectl rollout status.",
      "gen": "Any system where submitting and executing are separate: a job queued with no worker that can take it, an infrastructure plan waiting on capacity."
    },
    {
      "id": "heal",
      "tab": "Scenario 2",
      "short": "Delete vs crash",
      "q": "I delete a pod and it comes back. When my container crashes, it doesn't. Who reacts to what?",
